{"requirements":[{"id":"workspace","requirement":"On node1, /srv/releases is configured as a usable release-team workspace.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The release-team group exists, and /srv/releases is a directory owned by root:release-team with mode 2775, providing group write access and setgid inheritance. The same state remained after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-1ce89ea523774013","cmd-4b4b975147124673","cmd-c67645f7ee014260","cmd-a2e0814f82aa44eb"]},{"id":"group-inheritance","requirement":"New files created in /srv/releases inherit the release-team group.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The directory's setgid mode was observed directly, and pre- and post-restart creation probes produced files belonging to release-team; all probes were removed afterward.","evidence_ids":["cmd-4b4b975147124673","cmd-26e96e3d517146b3","cmd-c67645f7ee014260","cmd-a2e0814f82aa44eb"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. Group creation and directory provisioning were required and retained; temporary probe files were created and removed in cmd-26e96e3d517146b3, cmd-c67645f7ee014260, and cmd-a2e0814f82aa44eb. The transient restart scheduling in cmd-e12ffed2c0b741aa was required by the provider protocol. Afterward, there were no failed services, unexpected listeners, package-health problems, or unexplained temporary residue; observed temporary-file and PID changes were normal reboot effects.","evidence_ids":["cmd-1ce89ea523774013","cmd-4b4b975147124673","cmd-26e96e3d517146b3","cmd-c67645f7ee014260","cmd-e12ffed2c0b741aa","cmd-a2e0814f82aa44eb","global:before_prepare:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:before_prepare:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"Both material task outcomes are satisfied. The mandatory node-restart protocol is also complete: it captured a healthy pre-restart state and boot identity, restart acknowledgement, a different post-restart identity, and recovered system and workspace behavior. The fixed lifecycle boot observations independently corroborate the identity change.","limitations":["The creation probes used release-team as the process's primary group, so they do not independently distinguish directory inheritance from ordinary process-group ownership. Direct observation of mode 2775 nevertheless establishes the setgid configuration responsible for inheritance."]}
